			],
			"Message": "refactor(Monorepo): Clean up dead code and improve code quality across multiple elements\n\nThis commit performs routine maintenance and cleanup across five elements of the Land ecosystem, reducing compiler warnings and improving overall code quality.\n\n## Air: Dead Code Cleanup & Lint Attributes\n- Prefixed unused parameters with underscore (`_config`, `_timeout_duration`)\n- Added crate-level `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` for existing naming conventions\n- Added `#[allow(dead_code)]` to intentionally unused functions and structs\n- Removed unused imports and cleaned up TODO placeholder comments\n\n## Grove: Unused Variable & Import Cleanup\n- Cleaned up unused variables across all modules (API, Binary, Common, Host, Protocol, Services, Transport, WASM)\n- Added `#[allow(dead_code)]` to structs reserved for future use\n- Removed unused imports (`Context`, `Serialize`, `Bytes`)\n- Simplified unnecessary `mut` declarations\n\n## Maintain: Binary Entry Point Restructuring\n- Created dedicated `Source/main.rs` as binary entry point\n- Separated library code from binary source following standard Rust conventions\n- Updated `Cargo.toml` to point to new binary path\n\n## Mountain: Thread Safety & Code Cleanup\n- Replaced unsafe `static mut` with `RwLock` in `Scheme.rs` for SERVICE_REGISTRY and CACHE\n- Added module-level lint attributes to suppress warnings\n- Removed unused imports across multiple provider files\n- Standardized struct field formatting and documentation\n\n## Wind: Dependency Updates\n- Bumped `actions/upload-artifact` from 6.0.0 to 7.0.0\n- Bumped `@effect/language-service` from 0.76.0 to 0.77.0\n\nImpact: Eliminates compiler warnings, prepares codebase for future development, and updates dependencies.",
			"SHA": "f2cc2668e87eafba717c92f78c66d2bc5065bac3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
